1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,620
We don't have the evidence to build a case.

2
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,520
Not for lack of trying.

3
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:18,580
Mon as grunts walked.

4
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:20,980
Who the hell were those guys anyway?

5
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:23,620
They were just his hired muscle.

6
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:26,720
We did learn something from Chenbin's wife, though.

7
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:27,920
She met him.

8
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:29,840
He'd stopped by with Chen Jin.

9
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,460
I remember.

10
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:33,220
He was here to see Bean.

11
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,460
I called Bean to see if he was coming home.

12
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:38,560
He said no, but that he'd call Chen Jin later.

13
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:40,980
They didn't stay long after that.

14
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:42,920
Last thing.

15
00:00:43,860 --> 00:00:45,700
Is this the other man who was with Chen Jin?

16
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:47,400
That's him.

17
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:48,380
I'm sure.

18
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:51,960
I just assumed he worked for Chen Jin.

19
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:53,640
Oh, right.

20
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:56,800
He also moved the fruit to the kitchen before they left.

21
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:57,920
Oh, wait.

22
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:00,400
I was here the whole time he was in the kitchen.

23
00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:01,960
Could he have planted the money?

24
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:04,620
But why frame Chenbin?

25
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,160
I don't understand.

26
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:07,360
What's going on?

27
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,140
Is Captain Chen involved in this?

28
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:09,960
Maybe.

29
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,080
Maybe not.

30
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:13,720
It's still early in the investigation.

31
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:16,640
I'm still trying to make sense of what happened.

32
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:18,940
So is that all you can remember?

33
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:21,740
Right now, we need as many details as possible.

34
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:22,980
No matter how small.

35
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:25,120
Yes, that was everything.

36
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:26,660
I'm sorry.

37
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:30,080
I wish I could be more help.

38
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:33,020
Hey, what do you know about Chen Jin?

39
00:01:33,580 --> 00:01:34,500
Could it be him?

40
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:36,240
The one possessing people?

41
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:37,940
Sounds right.

42
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:40,100
He has the money to cover his tracks.

43
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:42,540
And his job is the perfect cover.

44
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:43,940
He can hide in plain sight.

45
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:49,640
It's not him.

46
00:01:50,220 --> 00:01:51,020
It couldn't be.

47
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,000
Trust me, I wouldn't know.

48
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:57,540
We started at the academy at the same time, then joined the force together.

49
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:00,880
Out of the two of us, he was the better cop.

50
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:04,120
To this day, I've never met a more dedicated officer.

51
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:09,960
He and I had a lot of cases that ended with him injured or nearly dead.

52
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:12,980
Which wouldn't have happened if he had a power like yours.

53
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:15,180
Eventually, we were reassigned.

54
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:19,240
We got new partners, new cases, and naturally grew apart.

55
00:02:20,060 --> 00:02:20,980
Until that day.

56
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:21,740
It's fine.

57
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:22,500
I'll drive.

58
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:25,560
Why don't you take a nap on the ride over to the crime scene?

59
00:02:26,140 --> 00:02:27,140
I appreciate it.

60
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:30,920
A woman was killed in her apartment in the Xiaoxing neighborhood.

61
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:48,200
We think it was a burglary.

62
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:51,680
The woman happened to be home, and things went wrong from there.

63
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:54,220
Captain, are you alright?

64
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:57,760
Jin Jin!

65
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:01,400
I want all of you out of here right now!

66
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:07,000
You shouldn't have been there, but I'd just taken over the case.

67
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:10,160
I didn't know his wife was the victim until after I was on the scene.

68
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:14,440
Later on, we learned that she was pregnant when she died.

69
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:17,160
Only a few weeks.

70
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,640
What happened to the burglar?

71
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:20,540
Did you catch him?

72
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:22,600
Yes, we did.

73
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:24,480
But that wasn't the end of it.

74
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:27,220
There wasn't enough evidence to convict him.

75
00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:29,780
So we managed to get away scot-free.

76
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:37,140
Then, about six months after his acquittal, he was found in his home, hanging from a noose.

77
00:03:38,220 --> 00:03:42,140
Police found a suicide note in which he confessed to both the burglary and the murder.

78
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,360
Not everyone believed it.

79
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:47,100
Some even suspected that Chun Jin had killed him.

80
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:50,100
That's when he left the force and started up his law firm.

81
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:53,860
We didn't speak after that.

82
00:03:54,560 --> 00:03:57,500
Now that I've seen what he's become, he feels like a stranger.

83
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,500
Tell me, have you found him yet?

84
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:14,160
You really are insane, you know that?

85
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:16,480
This plan is risky enough.

86
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:22,200
You're lucky that we still have a chance to pull this off, provided we remain one step ahead of the police.

87
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:25,320
We should find more people.

88
00:04:26,240 --> 00:04:27,300
Just to be safe.

89
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:29,140
Right. Yes, sir.

90
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:31,180
Captain Xiao, is that all?

91
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:34,680
While I appreciate the update, I doubt that's why you came to see us.

92
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:38,080
Right. About that, I need your help.

93
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,580
Huh? With what?

94
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:44,740
We found this on the hospital's surveillance footage.

95
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:48,580
Who is that?

96
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:50,140
Let me see.

97
00:04:56,060 --> 00:04:58,460
Lu Guang, this is right outside your room.

98
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,200
Who the hell is this, huh?

99
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,320
Hey, what are you hiding?

100
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:04,440
I know you know something.

101
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:06,960
It's all right.

102
00:05:07,380 --> 00:05:08,100
You're safe.

103
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,260
Please, tell us what happened.

104
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:18,360
Nothing happened.

105
00:05:18,940 --> 00:05:20,040
They just gave me this.

106
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:22,500
Who are they?

107
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:25,120
I honestly have no clue.

108
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:29,260
They didn't speak and they wore a mask, so I never saw their face.

109
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:38,520
Please!

110
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:48,620
As far as I can tell, it's just a photo.

111
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:54,320
The only unique things about it are the drawing and message on the back.

112
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:56,580
That's all I have.

113
00:05:56,580 --> 00:06:05,120
The note in the drawing appear to be left by a child.

114
00:06:06,120 --> 00:06:08,500
Might be the one in the photo, but we can't say.

115
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:11,600
It's said, can't lose my brother.

116
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:15,600
Maybe our mystery person wants us to find him for them?

117
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:17,720
Maybe.

118
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:21,260
Lu Guang, did you learn anything with your power?

119
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:23,620
No, nothing yet.

120
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,500
Maybe once I fully recovered.

121
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:27,740
Normally I have 12 hours to search.

122
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:30,720
But for now, I can't use my power that long.

123
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:34,320
Hey, I can do it.

124
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:37,860
I'll jump in and you guide me around like we always do.

125
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:40,240
I'd rather you not.

126
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:41,640
Too dangerous.

127
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,420
You can enter photos?

128
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:44,700
How's that work?

129
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:47,880
Well, it's essentially time travel.

130
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,940
Lu Guang sees the pass through photos,

131
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,300
while Chang Chaoshi possesses who takes them.

132
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:53,680
Time travel?

133
00:06:54,480 --> 00:06:55,460
That's amazing.

134
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,500
No case would go unsolved.

135
00:06:58,020 --> 00:06:58,940
It's not that easy.

136
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,640
You can do a lot of damage.

137
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:03,060
The world could come undone,

138
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,380
and you never know.

139
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,600
It's incredibly risky.

140
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:08,100
Hmm.

141
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:09,580
I hadn't thought of that.

142
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,340
The butterfly effect.

143
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:14,660
Can't imagine that kind of responsibility.

144
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:16,440
Not just that.

145
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:18,440
While the past can be changed,

146
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,800
you can't change everything.

147
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:44,820
What's done is done.

148
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:47,240
There's no point in fighting it.

149
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:48,580
But we have to.

150
00:07:48,580 --> 00:07:51,060
Because the future is still ours to make.

151
00:07:51,900 --> 00:07:53,060
You taught me that.

152
00:07:53,060 --> 00:08:00,720
That photo may be the key to solving all of this.

153
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:02,900
That alone should make it worth the risk.

154
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:05,680
Besides, Captain Xiao needs help.

155
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:08,040
And this is something that only you two can do.

156
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:09,360
Hmm.

157
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:14,420
All right.

158
00:08:14,860 --> 00:08:15,640
Just remember.

159
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:19,020
First, you get 12 hours.

160
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:23,380
Second, follow my lead and change nothing.

161
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:29,180
And third, past or future.

162
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:31,160
Must remain untouched.

163
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:35,280
I'll be damned.

164
00:08:36,540 --> 00:08:37,620
So that's it?

165
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:40,000
He just disappears and now he's in the past?

166
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:45,780
See?

167
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:47,940
It prints the photo by itself.

168
00:08:48,480 --> 00:08:49,200
Let's take a look.

169
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:50,380
Bring it here, please.

170
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:51,260
Kay.

171
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:53,260
Was that...

172
00:08:54,820 --> 00:08:56,480
Honey, did you just answer me?

173
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:58,140
But...

174
00:08:58,140 --> 00:08:58,540
Don't.

175
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,260
You're supposed to be mute.

176
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:02,220
Just keep your mouth shut from now on.

177
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:03,640
Fine.

178
00:09:03,900 --> 00:09:05,000
Wait, this kid is mute?

179
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:07,880
That's a good start, but we're gonna need more.

180
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:09,900
Look around you.

181
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:10,540
What's there?

182
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:11,660
Find something.

183
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:13,180
Anything that can tell you where you are.

184
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:13,980
Hey, calm down.

185
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:15,380
What are you hearing right now?

186
00:09:15,420 --> 00:09:16,280
Just let them work.

187
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:17,820
Remember, they're the experts.

188
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:19,260
They'll get you what you need.

189
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:19,940
Don't worry.

190
00:09:19,940 --> 00:09:21,760
Come on.

191
00:09:21,920 --> 00:09:22,320
Lu Guang?

192
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:22,960
Say something for me.

193
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:23,740
What should I do now?

194
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:24,840
I know you can do it.

195
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,260
Xiaxiu, please, try again.

196
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:31,560
Don't cry, sweetie.

197
00:09:32,140 --> 00:09:32,720
It's alright.

198
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,220
I pushed you hard.

199
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,840
Hey, I'm sorry, honey.

200
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:38,380
I won't do it anymore.

201
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:41,800
It's probably for the best that you take a break for the time being.

202
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:44,760
We'll find the secret behind the photo, but it's gonna take a while.

203
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:45,720
Right.

204
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:46,940
I'm sorry.

205
00:09:47,700 --> 00:09:48,900
This is all new to me.

206
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:50,740
Let's shift focus, then.

207
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:52,880
I could use your help, actually.

208
00:09:53,540 --> 00:09:55,820
Do you have any idea why I was the one possessed?

209
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,620
That answer is obvious.

210
00:09:58,300 --> 00:10:00,260
We know the killer's power needs photos.

211
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:02,820
So they got one of you.

212
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:05,000
The question is where they found it.

213
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,540
Um, I don't have a lot online.

214
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:10,280
My parents kept photo albums, but those are all physical.

215
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:14,520
They're not exactly tech savvy, so doubt it was them.

216
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:17,240
It doesn't have to be a picture of you, per se.

217
00:10:18,100 --> 00:10:19,760
It could be a group shot.

218
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,220
Oh, Shishan-shan?

219
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:26,260
But any photo with me would be on her phone.

220
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,460
Which Liu Min got a hold of.

221
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:30,740
While he was being controlled.

222
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:33,220
I'm calling her right now.

223
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:39,100
Hey, what's up?

224
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:40,880
Oh, did you hear about Liu Min?

225
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:41,700
You did.

226
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,160
So he really did it, then?

227
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:44,520
Well, but how?

228
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:45,340
Later, okay?

229
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:47,320
Right now, I need you to check your phone.

230
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:50,620
Do you have any pictures of me or ones where I'm in the background?

231
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,100
I think.

232
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,380
Hang on, I'll check.

233
00:10:53,380 --> 00:10:56,300
I'm not seeing one yet.

234
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:58,660
Maybe one with the two of us together.

235
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,560
I thought I had one.

236
00:11:03,060 --> 00:11:06,460
I took a selfie outside your studio, and you got caught in the background.

237
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:07,300
That's it.

238
00:11:07,900 --> 00:11:10,080
Captain Xiao, can you check something else?

239
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:12,700
I want to know if that photo was sent to anyone recently,

240
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:15,120
especially if it was to someone you don't recognize.

241
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,380
It would have been on the night that Liu Min was arrested.

242
00:11:19,960 --> 00:11:21,660
Yeah, I'm looking through my emails.

243
00:11:21,660 --> 00:11:23,580
I haven't found anything.

244
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,460
Check your text, then.

245
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:27,200
It could have been sent that way.

246
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:29,060
Hey, Lu Guang.

247
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:30,800
Where is this lady taking me?

248
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:32,820
As soon as I'm packed, we can head out.

249
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:33,940
All right?

250
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,380
This feels sudden.

251
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:37,620
Is it because I slipped up earlier?

252
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,080
Doubt it.

253
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:40,900
I can still see where you're going.

254
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:43,720
That tells me that nothing significant was changed.

255
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:47,160
I'm not finding anything.

256
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:50,240
Why is this so important to Chaolang?

257
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:53,000
The killer could have altered your phone's text history.

258
00:11:53,920 --> 00:11:54,320
Okay.

259
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:56,460
I'm sending her number to my people.

260
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:58,600
They can pull up her phone records.

261
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:03,580
Just wait, okay?

262
00:12:04,020 --> 00:12:05,720
Today is your follow-up with Dr. Qin.

263
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:07,600
Be a good girl while he takes a look.

264
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,980
It's been a while since her last treatment.

265
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:12,120
How has she been doing since then?

266
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,040
Amazing.

267
00:12:13,620 --> 00:12:15,220
Doctor, I heard her speak today.

268
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:16,880
I wish that you could have heard her.

269
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:18,920
That's wonderful.

270
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:22,400
Now that we know what works for her, we can tackle the problem head on.

271
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:26,600
This guy's a quack.

272
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:28,820
Hey, don't judge.

273
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:30,620
Everyone has their own beliefs, okay?

274
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:33,620
We don't have to agree or even understand.

275
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:34,980
Just respect it.

276
00:12:36,020 --> 00:12:37,940
This is why I keep telling you you should read.

277
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,880
The more you know, the more you can empathize.

278
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:43,300
He's so damn pedantic.

279
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:46,760
Does he treat everyone like that?

280
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:51,380
Luke Long is emotionally mature for someone his age.

281
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:54,780
These meds don't even have side effects listed.

282
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:56,600
Now then, let's see that hand.

283
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,880
Hey, there's nothing to be scared of.

284
00:12:59,140 --> 00:13:01,720
Once I check your pulse, I'll know the next step in your treatment.

285
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:11,180
This guy isn't going to notice me when he checks your pulse, right?

286
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:12,240
Really?

287
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:14,500
Now you believe in this stuff?

288
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:17,400
Hmm.

289
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:26,920
Hmm.

290
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:39,560
What is it?

291
00:13:39,940 --> 00:13:41,080
Is there something wrong?

292
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:47,720
This will sound strange, but her pulse is rather masculine for a girl.

293
00:13:47,980 --> 00:13:49,280
Almost as if she were a boy.

294
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:52,520
What does that mean, doctor?

295
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:53,520
Should I be worried?

296
00:13:54,460 --> 00:13:55,400
Well, no.

297
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:57,820
It means the medicine is working.

298
00:13:58,220 --> 00:14:00,520
Your daughter's pulse is getting stronger by the day.

299
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:03,640
That means stronger energy and stronger blood as well.

300
00:14:03,800 --> 00:14:05,820
Did this guy really just say stronger blood?

301
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:06,960
Incredible.

302
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:08,800
I don't know what to say.

303
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:09,720
Thank you.

304
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:10,480
Thank you.

305
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:17,320
Dr. Chin really is a miracle worker like everyone says.

306
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:20,140
He helped me hear my little Shishi speak today.

307
00:14:21,140 --> 00:14:22,640
We're on Dongmal Road.

308
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:25,080
There's a cyber cafe at the intersection.

309
00:14:26,220 --> 00:14:28,060
And a Yongshin salon across the street.

310
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:28,080
Dongmal Road.

311
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:28,700
Cyber cafe.

312
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:29,920
Yongshin salon.

313
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:32,620
We know the address for the doctor.

314
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,180
And based on the description he gave us,

315
00:14:36,180 --> 00:14:38,340
they're east of the Nande district right now.

316
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:42,880
We won't have anything specific until Cheng Xiaoshu finds a name and number for the neighborhood.

317
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:45,100
That's better than nothing.

318
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:47,600
We still don't know how any of this connects.

319
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:50,940
Oh, who this lost brother is.

320
00:14:51,940 --> 00:14:52,920
Stop for a second.

321
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:54,680
Then help carry the medicine.

322
00:14:55,620 --> 00:14:55,920
Huh?

323
00:14:56,620 --> 00:14:57,360
Right now?

324
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:58,540
Yes.

325
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:02,600
The child noticed that her mother was struggling and wanted to help.

326
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:08,560
What is it, Shishi?

327
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:11,600
Oh, thank you.

328
00:15:11,900 --> 00:15:13,320
But Mommy can handle it.

329
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:15,660
Don't.

330
00:15:15,660 --> 00:15:21,180
My, my.

331
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,800
You're just full of surprises today, aren't you?

332
00:15:24,020 --> 00:15:25,340
When did you get so strong?

333
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:26,760
Idiot.

334
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:28,320
Stop breaking character.

335
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:29,600
Get your head in the game.

336
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:54,760
If that girl wrote the known,

337
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:57,840
you'd think we'd have seen or heard about her brother by now, right?

338
00:15:57,840 --> 00:16:01,360
And what does she or her mom have to do with Tianjin or Liu Min?

339
00:16:02,980 --> 00:16:05,640
All we have is info, no context.

340
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,240
Hey, it's me.

341
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:10,240
Find anything?

342
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:11,800
What you did?

343
00:16:12,100 --> 00:16:13,380
Do we know what was sent then?

344
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,560
It was that thorough.

345
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:17,260
Well, can you recover anything?

346
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:18,820
Yeah, I can wait.

347
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:23,140
Who does the number belong to?

348
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:27,360
Almost.

349
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:28,200
There.

350
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:29,080
Good job.

351
00:16:38,620 --> 00:16:39,420
Oh, shoot.

352
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:40,940
We were so close.

353
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,680
Looks like we've got enough for one more try.

354
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:46,880
You ready?

355
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:51,440
I got this!

356
00:16:51,440 --> 00:17:00,440
Stupid red piece of crap!

357
00:17:01,220 --> 00:17:02,040
Hey, Shishi.

358
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:03,580
Look, I found more coins.

359
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:04,660
Let's try again.

360
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:08,340
Her name's Liu Lan.

361
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:11,000
She lived at 48 Tongli Lane in the Nandu district.

362
00:17:11,960 --> 00:17:12,440
Almost.

363
00:17:12,980 --> 00:17:13,480
Almost.

364
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:14,520
There you go.

365
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:15,420
Come on.

366
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:16,580
You're right there.

367
00:17:16,580 --> 00:17:17,440
That's it.

368
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:21,520
Weird thing is, records show she passed away a few years ago.

369
00:17:21,860 --> 00:17:22,120
Huh?

370
00:17:25,220 --> 00:17:26,140
Are you sure?

371
00:17:26,140 --> 00:17:31,160
Why would the text from Xu Shanshan's phone go to the number of a dead woman?

372
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:34,660
Sir, I only know what the phone company sent.

373
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:35,800
I double-checked it.

374
00:17:36,020 --> 00:17:37,360
This is some crazy shit.

375
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:39,500
Do we know anything about this Liu Lan?

376
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:43,360
Sir, you're going to have to wait on that.

377
00:17:43,660 --> 00:17:44,920
We've got a situation down here.

378
00:17:45,860 --> 00:17:46,440
Wait, what?

379
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,100
And they said they're a witness?

380
00:17:58,040 --> 00:17:58,440
Yes.

381
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,880
They're claiming they've seen everything on all our open cases.

382
00:18:01,880 --> 00:18:10,300
What else did they say?

383
00:18:10,940 --> 00:18:11,640
All right, then.

384
00:18:12,020 --> 00:18:14,000
Why don't you tell us everything from the beginning?

385
00:18:14,540 --> 00:18:14,700
What?

386
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:21,980
They said they'd only speak to Cheng Xiaoshu.

387
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:24,300
Oh, for an evil so unspoken.

